Chapter: SmpRiscvBoot

 A secondary hart executes guest code on RISC-V, checked from inside the
 guest. Under QEMU virt with -smp N -bios none every hart enters __start
 at reset; hart 0 boots normally, and a hart whose mhartid is non-zero
 branches to the AP path in the boot stub, stores 1 to the marker cell at
 0x80090000, and parks. That cell is written only by a core that ran our
 guest code -- for these backends, until now, none ever had. Reading it
 back non-zero is honest evidence a second hart is genuinely executing.
 A test showing that some computation finished proves nothing: hart 0
 alone can do that. This reads the cell a secondary alone can write.

Section: Probe

  ap-marker-addr : Integer = #80090000

  poll-ap : Integer -> Integer
  poll-ap (fuel) =
   if fuel <= 0 then 0
   else let v = peek-qword ap-marker-addr 0
   in if v /= 0 then 1
   else poll-ap (fuel - 1)

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    let ran = poll-ap 100000000
    in if ran /= 0 then print-line "an ap executed guest code"
    else print-line "AP DID NOT RUN"
  end
